{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"supersolar-classy-gecko","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A change can be permanently blocked by a stale LLM-Review -1\n\nWhen `LLM-Review` votes -1 for a reason that is later RESOLVED OUTSIDE the diff — the\n`bugfix-size-attestation` finding is the concrete case: it blocks on the ticket lacking a\nplan-review attestation, which is earned by running `rebar review-plan`, not by editing code —\nthere is no reliable way to get the vote recomputed. The change cannot land even though the\nfinding no longer holds.\n\n## The copy condition swallows every re-trigger\n    copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE OR changekind:MERGE_FIRST_PARENT_UPDATE\n                     OR changekind:TRIVIAL_REBASE\"\n\nObserved on change 1577 (bug 85fa), four attempts, all copied the stale -1 rather than\nre-reviewing:\n  1. `git commit --amend --no-edit` + push  -> same tree AND message -> NO_CODE_CHANGE -> copied\n  2. commit-MESSAGE-only amend + push      -> still NO_CODE_CHANGE (tree unchanged) -> copied\n  3. `recheck-review` comment (documented in docs/review-policy.md:47) -> the review bot did\n     not respond; it also CANCELLED the in-flight CI run, leaving a spurious Verified -1\n  4. rebase onto current main + push       -> TRIVIAL_REBASE -> copied\n\nCI behaves differently and correctly: `Verified` re-ran on patch sets 3 and 4. Only the LLM\nreview is stuck, which makes the asymmetry easy to miss.\n\nThe remaining levers per docs/review-policy.md are a maintainer re-trigger or a genuine\ncontent change. Manufacturing a code edit purely to defeat vote-copying is a bad incentive: it\nadds unreviewed churn to satisfy a mechanism, not a reviewer.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than working around\nThe gate stack already taxes small fixes. On 85fa: a ~70-line correctness fix hit the 800-line\nmodule cap, which forced a module extraction, which pushed it to 321 non-test lines, which\ntripped the 150-line bugfix floor, which required an LLM plan review to clear — and then the\nresulting -1 could not be recomputed once the attestation existed. Three gates compounding,\nwith no exit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A blocked author can cause LLM-Review to re-evaluate the CURRENT patch set without\n      changing code — e.g. `recheck-review` actually re-runs the reviewer, mirroring what\n      `recheck` does for CI.\n- [ ] If `recheck-review` is the intended mechanism, it works and is tested; if it is not,\n      docs/review-policy.md stops naming it.\n- [ ] A re-trigger comment does not CANCEL a running CI job (observed: posting\n      `recheck-review` cancelled run 31349189893 and produced a Verified -1 that reflected\n      cancellation, not a real failure).\n- [ ] Consider narrowing the copy condition: a finding whose evidence lives OUTSIDE the diff\n      (attestation state on the ticket) should not be copied forward across patch sets, since\n      the world it described can change without the tree changing.","id":"9b70-3108-706a-4483","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A resolved LLM-Review -1 cannot be re-evaluated: every re-trigger path hits a vote copy condition"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786375046629006001,"uuid":"e10055db-f440-4b15-ab33-2db6a81890a6"}